        "market_blurb": "Pottstown, Pennsylvania, a former steel and iron manufacturing hub along the Schuylkill River, has transitioned into a regional center for healthcare, education, and light manufacturing. Tower Health's Pottstown Hospital and the Pottstown School District are among the borough's largest employers, while legacy industrial firms and logistics companies continue to anchor the local economy. The historic downtown and surrounding Montgomery County suburbs support a mix of small businesses and service industries catering to homeowners and renters alike.",
        "local_note": "In and around Pottstown, the most problematic pests are carpenter ants, Eastern subterranean termites, brown marmorated stink bugs, and deer ticks (a Lyme disease concern in wooded and suburban yards), with occasional bed bug issues in multi-family housing. Activity is strongly seasonal, peaking from spring through fall, though stink bugs and rodents commonly invade homes seeking warmth in late autumn and winter.",
